Boards that select the GXL glue variant never run usb3_init(), so the glue's
USB_R1_U3H_HOST_PORT_POWER_CONTROL_PRESENT bit stays clear and HCC_PPC reads 0
although the controller really does switch port power.

Measured on this board: vendor reports hcc_params 0x0228fe6c (PPC = 1),
mainline reports 0x0228fe64 (PPC = 0). Only bit 3 differs.

The opt-in sits on the glue node, which is not the device xhci probes for,
so it is looked up by compatible.

diff -ruN a/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c	2026-11-19 22:37:02
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c	2026-11-19 22:37:02
@@ -5474,6 +5474,21 @@
 	xhci->hcc_params = readl(&xhci->cap_regs->hcc_params);
 	if (xhci->hci_version > 0x100)
 		xhci->hcc_params2 = readl(&xhci->cap_regs->hcc_params2);
+	{
+		/*
+		 * Boards that select the GXL glue variant never run usb3_init(), so
+		 * the glue's PORT_POWER_CONTROL_PRESENT bit stays clear and HCC_PPC
+		 * reads 0 although the controller does switch port power (vendor
+		 * firmware reports PPC = 1). The opt-in lives on the glue node, not
+		 * on the dwc3 child that xhci probes for.
+		 */
+		struct device_node *glue =
+			of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL,
+						"amlogic,meson-gxl-usb-ctrl");
+		if (glue && of_property_read_bool(glue,
+						  "amlogic,port-power-control"))
+			xhci->hcc_params |= (1 << 3);
+	}
 
 	xhci->dma_mask_bits = 64;
 	xhci->max_slots = HCS_MAX_SLOTS(hcs_params1);
